hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"983","1018 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not right for a Muslim man who spends two nights with something to bequeath concerning, except that his will is written with him."
"984","1019 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Amir ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I fell ill in Makkah with an illness from which I nearly died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have much wealth, and none inherits from me except my daughter; shall I bequeath two-thirds of my wealth? He said: No. I said: Then half? He said: No. I said: Then a third? He said: A third, and a third is much. If you leave your heirs rich, it is better than leaving them dependent."
"985","1020 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayyah, informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man freed six slaves of his at the time of his death, owning no wealth besides them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called them, divided them into thirds, cast lots among them, freed two and kept four enslaved. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke stern words to him."
"986","1021 - Abu Ayyub Sulayman ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Bahrani narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jabir narrated to us, and Salim ibn Amir and others narrated to me, from Abu Umamah and others who witnessed the sermon of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that day. Among what he said was: Indeed Allah has given every rightful one his right; there is no bequest for an heir."
"987","1022 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger judged debts before bequests, though you recite: after any bequest he bequeaths or debt. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged inheritance for full brothers, to the exclusion of half-brothers through the father."
"988","1023 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj and Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, they said: Abadah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, regarding His word: And whoever is poor, let him eat honorably. He said: It was revealed concerning the guardian of the orphan who manages him and stands over him: if he is needy, he may eat from it."
"989","1024 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am poor, I own nothing, and I have an orphan. He said: Eat from your orphan's wealth without extravagance, wastefulness, or hoarding."
